==============================================================
## 1. What the kernel checks
==============================================================

The DRM core validates every plane at drm_dev_register(). Upstream
drivers/gpu/drm/drm_mode_config.c:

$ sed -n 867,885p /mega/tmp/kp_drm_mode_config.c
static void validate_blend_mode_for_alpha_formats(struct drm_plane *plane)
{
	const struct drm_format_info *fmt;
	u32 i;

	/* blend mode property supported, no need to check anything */
	if (plane->blend_mode_property)
		return;

	for (i = 0; i < plane->format_count; i++) {
		fmt = drm_format_info(plane->format_types[i]);
		if (fmt->has_alpha) {
			drm_warn(plane->dev,
				 "[PLANE:%d:%s] pixel format with alpha exposed but blend mode not setup. Please fix.\n",
				 plane->base.id, plane->name);
			break;
		}
	}
}
[exit 0]

A plane that advertises an alpha format must carry blend_mode_property,
otherwise this drm_warn fires. The driver exposed ARGB8888 on the cursor
plane with no property at all, so the warning was correct and the fix is
to describe the hardware truthfully, not to hide the format.

