--- src/sm750_drm.c: the include
$ sed -n 28,32p src/sm750_drm.c
#include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
#include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
#include <drm/drm_blend.h>
#include <drm/drm_connector.h>
#include <drm/drm_crtc_helper.h>
[exit 0]

--- src/sm750_drm.c: the cursor plane setup, with the justification comment
$ sed -n 3460,3500p src/sm750_drm.c
	sdev->pipe.crtc.funcs = &sm750_crtc_funcs;
#endif
	if (sdev->hardware_cursor) {
		ret = drm_universal_plane_init(drm, &sdev->cursor_plane,
				drm_crtc_mask(&sdev->pipe.crtc),
				&sm750_cursor_plane_funcs, cursor_formats,
				ARRAY_SIZE(cursor_formats), NULL,
				DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR, "sm750-cursor");
		if (ret)
			return ret;
		drm_plane_helper_add(&sdev->cursor_plane,
				     &sm750_cursor_plane_helper_funcs);
		/*
		 * The cursor plane exposes DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, so the DRM core
		 * requires a blend mode property: drm_mode_config_validate()
		 * warns "pixel format with alpha exposed but blend mode not
		 * setup" for a plane that advertises an alpha format without
		 * one. The hardware still consumes per-pixel alpha - it becomes
		 * a dithered transparent/opaque mask over three palette entries
		 * (sm750_cursor_encode) - so hiding alpha by switching to
		 * XRGB8888 would misdescribe the cursor and break compositors
		 * that hand us ARGB8888. PREMULTI is the one mode that is true
		 * here: ARGB8888 colour is premultiplied, and
		 * sm750_cursor_unpremultiply() divides alpha back out before
		 * quantising. COVERAGE is deliberately not offered because it
		 * would claim the driver premultiplies colour it receives
		 * unpremultiplied, which it does not. PREMULTI is also the only
		 * mode every supported kernel accepts (6.17 rejects a mask
		 * without it), so no version guard is needed. No plane alpha
		 * property is created: the hardware has no plane-wide alpha.
		 */
		ret = drm_plane_create_blend_mode_property(&sdev->cursor_plane,
				BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI));
		if (ret)
			return ret;
		sdev->pipe.crtc.cursor = &sdev->cursor_plane;
		drm->mode_config.cursor_width = SM750_DRM_CURSOR_WIDTH;
		drm->mode_config.cursor_height = SM750_DRM_CURSOR_HEIGHT;
	}
	ret = drm_vblank_init(drm, 1);
	if (ret)
[exit 0]

The format list is unchanged (cursor_formats[] at src/sm750_drm.c:3424 is
still DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888) and the palette conversion path is unchanged:
sm750_cursor_unpremultiply() at src/sm750_drm.c:2618, alpha_dither[] at
:2714, and the enable message at :3807 still says
'64x64 hardware cursor plane enabled with ARGB palette conversion'.

==============================================================
## 3. The gate: the check is stronger, not weaker
==============================================================

$ sed -n 20,50p tests/check-hardware-cursor.sh
	'sm750_cursor_unpremultiply' \
	'sm750_cursor_palette' \
	'sm750_cursor_encode' \
	'bool cursor_image_valid;' \
	'bool rebuild_image;' \
	'state->fb != old_state->fb' \
	'state->fb_damage_clips != old_state->fb_damage_clips' \
	'output_width != sdev->cursor_encoded_width' \
	'if (rebuild_image) {' \
	'value << ((x & 3) * 2)' \
	'SM750_DRM_HWC_ADDRESS_ENABLE |' \
	'64x64 hardware cursor plane enabled with ARGB palette conversion' \
	'#include <drm/drm_blend.h>' \
	'drm_plane_create_blend_mode_property(&sdev->cursor_plane,' \
	'BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI)'; do
	grep -F "$requirement" "$source_file" >/dev/null || {
		echo "Missing hardware-cursor requirement: $requirement" >&2
		exit 1
	}
done

# The cursor plane advertises ARGB8888, so the DRM core requires a blend mode
# property (drm_mode_config_validate). The hardware has no plane-wide alpha, so
# exposing drm_plane_create_alpha_property would promise a blend the driver
# cannot perform - fail if it appears.
if grep -F 'drm_plane_create_alpha_property' "$source_file" >/dev/null; then
	echo "Cursor plane must not expose a plane alpha property" >&2
	exit 1
fi

awk '
[exit 0]

$ ./tests/check-hardware-cursor.sh
Hardware cursor plane checks passed
[exit 0]

Three requirements were added and one negative assertion: the blend
property must be created, PREMULTI must be offered, and
drm_plane_create_alpha_property must NOT appear (the hardware has no
plane-wide alpha, so advertising one would be a second mismatch). The
script failed red against the pre-fix driver.

