[exit 0]

Same declaration and same enum values in every tree, so the call needs no
LINUX_VERSION_CODE guard. 6.17 additionally rejects a mask without
PREMULTI (WARN_ON in drivers/gpu/drm/drm_blend.c), which is why PREMULTI
is in the mask rather than an empty one; the newer trees accept it too.

==============================================================
## 6. The running kernel really performs this check
==============================================================

The installed module cannot be replaced from this task (no root; T11
installs the rebuilt 0.6.0). What can be shown is that the kernel now
running contains the check and the property it looks for:

$ bash -c dd if=/boot/vmlinuz-7.3.4-100.fc43.x86_64 bs=1 skip=21196 2>/dev/null | zstd -d -c 2>/dev/null | strings -a | grep -n 'pixel format with alpha exposed\|pixel blend mode\|Pre-multiplied\|^Coverage$'
335187:[drm] [PLANE:%d:%s] pixel format with alpha exposed but blend mode not setup. Please fix.
363102:pixel blend mode
363103:Pre-multiplied
363104:Coverage
[exit 0]

The warning string, the property name and both enum labels are in the
image. With blend_mode_property set, validate_blend_mode_for_alpha_formats()
returns at its first line and the warning cannot be emitted.

