Every warning is host tooling (pahole or compiler version), none from src/.

==============================================================
## 11. What this does and does not prove
==============================================================

Proved here: the driver creates the property the core check keys on, the
property offers the mode the hardware implements, the object and all four
kernel builds carry it, and no check regressed.

NOT proved here, because this task cannot load a module: the live warning
disappears only when T11 installs the rebuilt 0.6.0 module and the host
reboots or reloads it. The pre-fix capture is
docs/evidence/runtime/cursor-alpha-01-warning-before.txt; the post-install
capture belongs to T11 and must be taken with
sudo -n /usr/bin/dmesg | grep -n 'sm750-cursor'.
